Maize COs taken from: 10.1073/pnas.1413864112.
Teosinte COs taken from: https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2112970118

This .R code details how to read in maize & teosinte crossover events, filter based on resolution, number of COs per individual, and normalize by population size. 
.R also has code related to finding the distances of COs to the nearest telomere (based on B73 v4 coordinates) and is able to calculate a genetic map based on COs between SNPs, with a physical map provided.
At the end, there is ggplot code to plot CO events and recombination rates across the 10 chromosomes of maize & teosinte.
